hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"342","Narrated by Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala Al-Attar, narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. H and us Ahmad bin Abdah, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, and Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. H and us Abdul Jabbar, once, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. H and Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed the evening prayer one night, so Omar went out and said: Prayers, O Messenger of God! The women and children lay down, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out with water dripping from his head while he was wiping it from his two parts. He says: “If it were not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to pray at this hour.” One of them said: The time has come, unless I make it difficult for my nation. This is the wording of the hadith of Abdul Jabbar when he combined the hadith, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj and Amr. Ibn Dinar, and he said when he reported the news of Ibn Jurayj: “It is time, had I not made it difficult for my nation,” and Ahmad Ibn Abdah said: “If I had not made it difficult “I have commanded the believers to pray this prayer at this hour.”"
"343","Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, became blind. At dinner one night, Omar called him and said: The women and children were asleep, so he went out to them and said: “No one is waiting for this prayer.” “From the people of the earth other than you.” Al-Zuhri said: No one was praying that day except those in Medina."
"344","On the authority of Yusuf bin Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: One night we were waiting for the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him for the last evening prayer, so he came out to us until a third of the night had passed, and we do not know what he occupied with his family or others. So, he said when he left: “You are waiting for a prayer that people of no other religion are waiting for, and had it not been a burden on my nation, I would have prayed this prayer with them.” The hour.” Then he ordered the muezzin to establish the prayer and he prayed."
"345","We are Bundar, we are Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Dawud. H and Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz told us, about Abdul-Warith, about Dawood. H. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri. He said: We waited for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the evening prayer until half of the night had passed, then he came and led us in prayer, then he said: “Take Your seats, for the people have taken their resting places, and you will not cease in prayer since you have been waiting for it, were it not for the weakness of the weak, the sickness of the sick, and the need of the Needless to say, I would have delayed this prayer until the middle of the night.” This is the hadith of Bundar"
